module examples.err_cap_actor_enum_field

# plans/M7.md item I (the adversarial sweep), 03-hardware.md §1: "`@actor`
# structs cannot hold capabilities in fields, parameters, messages, or
# captures."
#
# `golden/err-cap-actor-field` already pins that rule "at any nesting"
# through an array of a plain data *struct*. This is the same sentence
# through an **enum variant payload**, which item A's walk could not see
# at all: `type_contains_capability` consulted a
# `BTreeMap<String, &DeclStruct>`, so `structs.get("Holder")` was `None`
# for every enum and the recursion simply stopped there. The declaration
# below compiled clean before item I.
#
# One missing map entry, five rules failing open at once — each pinned by
# its own sibling golden here: `err-cap-enum-return` (§1's unforgeability
# floor), `err-cap-enum-driver-export` (§1's "never raw capabilities"),
# `err-cap-provenance-enum` (§1's provenance sentence),
# `err-mmio-alias-enum` (§2's no-alias rule) and
# `err-actor-handle-in-enum-message` (02-language.md §9.1, an M6 rule with
# the identical hole). `sema::types::components_by_name` is the one table
# all of them now read.

struct VirtioBlock:
    id: u32

enum Holder:
    Armed(DeviceCap[VirtioBlock])
    Idle(u32)

@actor
pub struct Sink:
    held: Holder
    n: u32
